      "message": "finalize is deprecated and oiverriding it is discouraged unless you really know what you\u0027re doing. In this case I don\u0027t think this will ever run because unless you call unregisterStateCallback, the system server will maintain a live reference to mCallback through a binder proxy, and because mCallback is not static it will maintain a reference to the EnabledStateListener, and the object will never be garbage collected. This will leak memory both here and in the system server until this process exits.",
